{
 "name": "reflectron TOF (oa, refined: WM-matched, mirror-imaged)",
 "notes": "Domain trimmed to the active region: x sliced to [55, 95] mm of the original frame and re-zeroed (x' = x - 55); 0-55 mm was field-free vacuum. All x positions in the notes below are the OLD frame. Source plates are clipped at the new left edge; certification below proves the beam-region field is unchanged. REQUIRES ion_gym >= v329 (generate_births beam+temperature SUPERPOSITION, 2026-08-11). On v328 and earlier, temperature_k > 0 replaces the 2 eV beam entirely: ions get no sideways drift, miss the detector, and cycle between the static source field and the mirror -- seen as repeated reflections with source re-entry every ~6.8 us (m/z 100) / ~15.2 us (m/z 500). That is the version mismatch speaking, not the design. REFINED oa-TOF: the toy example's chain with the two first-order design rules actually APPLIED instead of compensated. Derivation: (1) Wiley-McLaren: with E1 chosen at 250 V/mm (the toy's 15 V/mm made turn-around ~ the whole packet width at 300 K) and U_tot 4000 eV, the first-order space focus lands D_s = 27.9 mm past G2 (y = 55.9). (2) Single-stage mirror: first-order energy focus images that plane onto the detector when L1+L2 = 4*penetration; L1 112.1 + L2 136.5 mm gives pen 62.1 mm, E_mir = U_tot/pen = 64.37 V/mm. The ladder is one rule, not 26 magic numbers. Ring pitch is scaled 1.4 -> 4.0 mm so the inter-ring gap is 4 cells at the 0.5 mm solve (the toy's 1-cell gap is why its V_back optimum was erratic under refinement). Source carries a REAL 300 K temperature superposed on the 2 eV beam (turn-around is now in the model, ~1.3/2.9 ns for m/z 100/500) and the packet is squeezed to 0.5 mm in y. STILL DELIBERATELY TOY-ADJACENT: gridded (3 transmission grids + transparent rings), single-stage (first-order energy focus only), 2-D. Next steps if pursued: two-segment ladder for second-order (Mamyrin), then gridless. OPERATING POINT (all derived, see notes): E1 250.0 V/mm, E2 208.33 V/mm (V_push 5500, G1 2500, G2 0), U_tot 4000 eV, source 300 K beam 2 eV, packet 3.0 x 0.5 mm at y=10; mirror 26 rings pitch 4.0 mm (gap 2.0 mm = 4 cells at 0.5 mm), E_mir 64.37 V/mm, V_back 7017 V, single-stage LINEAR ladder V(y)=E_mir*(y-y_ent). Predicted (analytic, this file's geometry): m/z 100 lands x 77.5 mm at 6.37 us; m/z 500 x 77.5 mm at 14.24 us. Numbers from flights must be re-measured and quoted WITH cell size. MEASURED (2026-08-11, 24 ions/mass, seed 1): 48/48 on detector at BOTH 0.5 and 0.25 mm cells; m/z 100 TOF 6.3671 us FWHM 1.34 ns (R=t/2dt 2383), m/z 500 TOF 14.2371 us FWHM 2.98 ns (R 2390); refining 0.5 -> 0.25 mm moves TOF by 0.007% and FWHM by <= 0.04 ns (CONVERGED; the toy moved R 372 -> 65 under the same refinement). Measured FWHM equals the predicted turn-around limit (1.31 / 2.93 ns) -- the residual is the term single-stage focusing cannot remove, i.e. the design rules are exhausted, not misapplied. Ideal 1-D audit: dT/dy0 = +0.0 ns/mm at the designed E_mir. SIGMA CONVENTION: the certified FWHM/R above use population sigma (ddof=0); the GUI's arrival-time table uses sample sigma (n-1), ~2% wider at n=24 (R 2333/2340 vs 2383/2390). Same flight, same physics -- quote whichever, with its convention. COOLED OPERATING POINT (2026-08-11, step 1 of the boost plan; source 77 K per the collisionally cooled quad front end, all else unchanged, 0.5 mm cells, population sigma): m/z 100 24/24, TOF 6.3671 us, FWHM 0.76 ns, R 4195; m/z 500 24/24, TOF 14.2372 us, FWHM 1.82 ns, R 3908. Predicted turn-around at 77 K: 0.66 / 1.48 ns. The 300 K numbers above remain the certified hot point. | L-218 SUB-CELL FIX (2026-09-03): pitch 0.5 -> 0.25 mm so the declared source spans the 2.0-cell advisory line (was 1.00 cells); the prior numbers were exposed to the unresolved-packet-derivative failure mode L-216 measured (5x aberration inflation at 0.19 cells). The advisory line is not proof of convergence; quote packet derivatives from a pitch ladder.",
